<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Choiseul Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lauru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Choiseul is an island in the north-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, lying south-east of Bougainville. Part of the German Solomon Islands from 1886, it was transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with Santa Isabel and other islands under an agreement of 1899, taking effect in 1900. It is now Choiseul Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/choiseul-island.jpg" alt="Choiseul Island" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sadalmelik · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Choiseul_Topography.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
